{"id":921,"date":"2014-06-06T13:42:03","date_gmt":"2014-06-06T13:42:03","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/?page_id=921"},"modified":"2015-05-18T20:18:01","modified_gmt":"2015-05-18T20:18:01","slug":"useful-info","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/workshops\/berlin2014\/useful-info\/","title":{"rendered":"Useful info"},"content":{"rendered":"<p><span class=\"STYLE29\"><br \/>\n<\/span><\/p>\n<div>\n<h1 class=\"STYLE29\">Welcome to Berlin<\/h1>\n<table cellspacing=\"5\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td valign=\"top\">Welcome to Berlin, a world city of culture, politics, media, and science. Berlin is the capital city of Germany, and, with a population of 3.49 million people, Germany&#8217;s largest city. Located in northeastern Germany, it is the center of the Berlin-Brandenburg Metropolitan Region, which has 4.4 million residents from over 190 nations. Located in the European Plains, Berlin is influenced by a temperate seasonal climate. Around one third of the city&#8217;s area is composed of forests, parks, gardens, rivers and lakes.<a href=\"http:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Berlin\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">[source: Wikipedia]<\/a><\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td valign=\"top\"><a href=\"http:\/\/www.seminaris.de\/en\/hotels\/seminaris-campushotel-berlin\/accommodation.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Seminaris Campus Hotel<\/strong> (Tutorials and Workshop venue) <\/a> is located directly on the campus of the Freie Universtit\u00e4t Berlin. <strong>The most convenient option for conference attendees is to stay in the Seminaris Campus<\/strong>..<\/p>\n<p lang=\"EN-US\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">You can make your reservation request at the Seminaris Campus hotel either by Tel.: +49 30 5577 97-0, email: <\/span><a title=\"mailto:berlin@seminaris.de\" href=\"mailto:berlin@seminaris.de\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">berlin@seminaris.de<\/span><\/a><span lang=\"EN-US\">, or <a href=\"http:\/\/www.seminaris.de\/en\/hotels\/seminaris-campushotel-berlin\/reservation-request.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">web form request<\/a><\/span><\/p>\n<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td valign=\"top\"><a href=\"http:\/\/www.zib.de\/contact\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Konrad-Zuse-Zentrum f\u00fcr Informationstechnik Berlin (ZIB)<\/strong> (Hackathon venue) <\/a> is located in Takustrasse 7, D-14195 Berlin<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p><strong>Maps and Directions<\/strong>: <a title=\"Maps and Directions\" href=\"http:\/\/www.mi.fu-berlin.de\/en\/fb\/contact\/location.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">http:\/\/www.mi.fu-berlin.de\/en\/fb\/contact\/location.html<\/a><\/p>\n<p>You can plan your public transport journey with the BVG journey planer\u00a0 <a title=\"http:\/\/www.bvg.de\" href=\"http:\/\/www.bvg.de\/en\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">www.bvg.de<\/a><\/p>\n<h2 class=\"STYLE29\">Arriving by Train<\/h2>\n<p><strong>from Berlin Hauptbahnhof (Main Station):<\/strong><br \/>\nS5, S7, S75 or S9, Station: Zoologischer Garten (ZOO)<br \/>\nUnderground U9, Station: Rathaus Steglitz (last station of the U9)<br \/>\nBus X83, Station: Museen Dahlem (ca. 4-5 stops from Rathaus Steglitz)<\/p>\n<p>You can plan your public transport journey with the BVG journey planer\u00a0 <a title=\"http:\/\/www.bvg.de\" href=\"http:\/\/www.bvg.de\/en\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">www.bvg.de<\/a><\/p>\n<p>For your train connection within Germany you can use the\u00a0<a title=\"http:\/\/reiseauskunft.bahn.de\/bin\/query.exe\/dn?searchMode=ADVANCED&amp;start=1&amp;S=&amp;Z=14195%20Berlin%2C%20K%F6nigin-Luise-Stra%DFe%2024&amp;ZADR=1&amp;date=&amp;time=&amp;timesel=depart&amp;application=PRIVATETRANSPORT\" href=\"http:\/\/reiseauskunft.bahn.de\/bin\/query.exe\/dn?searchMode=ADVANCED&amp;start=1&amp;S=&amp;Z=14195%20Berlin%2C%20K%F6nigin-Luise-Stra%DFe%2024&amp;ZADR=1&amp;date=&amp;time=&amp;timesel=depart&amp;application=PRIVATETRANSPORT\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Deutsche Bahn<\/a> portal.<\/p>\n<div>\n<h2 class=\"STYLE29\">Arriving by Airplane<\/h2>\n<p>Berlin&#8217;s two airports Tegel (TXL) and Sch\u00f6nefeld (SXF) are connected to many major cities in Europe and to world-wide destinations via Germany&#8217;s air traffic hubs Frankfurt and Munich.<\/p>\n<p><strong>From Tegel (TXL):<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>By taxi: A taxi ride from Tegel airport to Berlin-Dahlem takes about 20 minutes and costs approximately 30 Euros.<\/p>\n<p>By public transport: A ride to the conference venue (subway station &#8220;Dahlem-Dorf&#8221;) by bus and subway takes about 35 minutes and costs 2.30 Euros (zone AB).<\/p>\n<p>The bus station is located at the entrance to the main hall (terminals A and B).<\/p>\n<table frame=\"border\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>From<\/strong><\/td>\n<td><strong>Line<\/strong><\/td>\n<td><strong>Direction<\/strong><\/td>\n<td><strong>Get off at<br \/>\n<\/strong><\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Tegel airport<\/td>\n<td><strong>X9<\/strong> (Bus)<\/td>\n<td>Zoologischer Garten<\/td>\n<td><strong>Jakob-Kaiser-Platz<\/strong> (~4 mins.)<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Jakob-Kaiser-Platz<\/td>\n<td><strong>U 7<\/strong> (subway, &#8220;U-Bahn&#8221;)<\/td>\n<td>Rudow<\/td>\n<td><strong>Fehrbelliner Platz<\/strong> (~11 mins.)<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fehrbelliner Platz<\/td>\n<td><strong>U 3<\/strong> (subway, &#8220;U-Bahn&#8221;)<\/td>\n<td>Krumme Lanke<\/td>\n<td><strong>Dahlem-Dorf<\/strong> (~8 mins.)<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<p>You need to buy a ticket for <strong>zones AB<\/strong> at one of the ticket machines available at the bus station or directly from the bus driver. <strong>Do not forget to stamp your ticket using the yellow ticket validation machine.<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>From Sch\u00f6nefeld (SXF):<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>By taxi: A taxi ride from Sch\u00f6nefeld airport to Berlin-Dahlem takes 30 minutes and costs approximately 40 Euros.<\/p>\n<p>By train: Berlin Sch\u00f6nefeld Airport is connected to Berlin&#8217;s regional railway system. A ride to the conference venue takes 45 minutes and costs 3.00 Euros (zone ABC).<\/p>\n<p>Please note that until further progress of the new airport infrastructure, the S-Bahn station remains in 10 minutes <strong>walking<\/strong> distance from the arrival hall.<\/p>\n<p>In order to get to Berlin-Dahlem, you need to change trains twice:<\/p>\n<div>\n<table frame=\"border\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>From<\/strong><\/td>\n<td><strong>Line<\/strong><\/td>\n<td><strong>Direction<\/strong><\/td>\n<td><strong>Get off at<\/strong><\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Airport train station<br \/>\ntrack 13<\/td>\n<td><strong>S 45<\/strong> (suburban train, &#8220;S-Bahn&#8221;)<\/td>\n<td>Bundesplatz<\/td>\n<td><strong>S\u00fcdkreuz<\/strong> (~21 mins.)<br \/>\ntrack 11<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>S\u00fcdkreuz<br \/>\ntrack 11<\/td>\n<td><strong>S 41 <\/strong>(S-Bahn)<strong><br \/>\n<\/strong><\/td>\n<td>Ringbahn<\/td>\n<td><strong>Heidelberger Platz<\/strong> (~7 mins.)<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Heidelberger Platz<\/td>\n<td><strong>U 3<\/strong> (subway, &#8220;U-Bahn&#8221;)<\/td>\n<td>Krumme Lanke<\/td>\n<td><strong>Dahlem-Dorf<\/strong> (~6 mins.)<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>\n<p>You need to buy a ticket for <strong>zones ABC<\/strong> at one of the ticket machines available at the the lower level of the train station. <strong>Do not forget to stamp your ticket using the yellow ticket validation machine.<\/strong><\/p>\n<\/div>\n<div>\n<h1 class=\"STYLE29\">Alternative Hotels in the Area<\/h1>\n<p><strong class=\"STYLE28\">Best Western Premier Hotel Steglitz International (****)<\/strong><br \/>\nAlbrechtstrasse 2<br \/>\n12165 Berlin<br \/>\nHomepage: <a href=\"http:\/\/www.si-hotel.com\/default.aspx?lang=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">www.si-hotel.com<\/a><br \/>\n7 minutes bus trip from hotel to conference venue<\/p>\n<p><strong>Steigenberger Hotel Berlin (*****<\/strong>)<br \/>\nLos-Angeles-Platz 1<br \/>\n10789 Berlin<br \/>\nTel.: +49 (0) 30 &#8211; 21 27 0<br \/>\nHomepage: <a href=\"http:\/\/www.steigenberger.com\/en\/Berlin\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">www.steigenberger.com<\/a><br \/>\n12 minutes by subway (direct connection)<\/p>\n<p><strong>Alsterho (f****)<\/strong><br \/>\nAugsburger Stra\u00dfe 5<br \/>\n10789 Berlin<br \/>\nTel.: +49 (0) 30 &#8211; 21 24 27 19<br \/>\nHomepage: <a href=\"http:\/\/www.alsterhof.com\/nc\/en\/hotel\/home.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">www.alsterhof.com<br \/>\n<\/a>12 minutes by subway (direct connection)<\/p>\n<p><strong>Best Western Hotel President (****<\/strong>)<br \/>\nAn der Urania 16-18<br \/>\n10787 Berlin<br \/>\nHomepage: <a href=\"http:\/\/www.hotel-president-berlin.de\/default.aspx?lang=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">www.hotel-president-berlin.de<\/a><br \/>\n14 minutes by subway (direct connection)<\/p>\n<h2 class=\"STYLE29\">Hostels<\/h2>\n<p><strong>Happy Bed Hostel<\/strong><br \/>\nK\u00f6rnerstra\u00dfe 53<br \/>\n12169 Berlin<br \/>\nHomepage: <a href=\"http:\/\/www.happybed.de\/en\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">www.happybed.de<\/a><\/p>\n<p>7 minutes bus trip from hostel to conference venue<\/p>\n<p>Single room with en suite bathroom 30 \u20ac \/with shared bathroom 19,50 \u20ac per person\/night<br \/>\nDouble room 25 \u20ac \/ 15,50 \u20ac per person\/night<br \/>\nTriple (shared bathroom only) 14,50 \u20ac per person\/night<br \/>\n4-6 beds\/room 11 \u20ac per person\/night<br \/>\nBreakfast, bed linnen, cleaning, and taxes included.<\/p>\n<h2 class=\"STYLE29\">Further Information<\/h2>\n<p>There are more than 700 hotels and hostels located in Berlin. For more information, please refer to Berlin&#8217;s official tourist information web site at <a href=\"http:\/\/hotel.berlin.de\/vacancyForm.jsp?sprache=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">http:\/\/hotel.berlin.de<\/a>.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Welcome to Berlin Welcome to Berlin, a world city of culture, politics, media, and science. Berlin is the capital city of Germany, and, with a population of 3.49 million people, Germany&#8217;s largest city. Located in northeastern Germany, it is the &hellip; <a href=\"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/workshops\/berlin2014\/useful-info\/\">Continue reading <span class=\"meta-nav\">&rarr;<\/span><\/a><\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":274,"parent":911,"menu_order":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","template":"","meta":{"footnotes":""},"class_list":["post-921","page","type-page","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/921","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/page"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=921"}],"version-history":[{"count":14,"href":"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/921\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":1077,"href":"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/921\/revisions\/1077"}],"up":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/911"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/274"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.swat4ls.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=921"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}